Nomination and Remuneration Committee
the Nomination and Remuneration Committee are as specified in Section 178 of the Companies Act, 2013, Regulation 19 read with Schedule II Part-D of Listing Regulations (except to the extent of exemptions provided to Govt. Companies). The Nomination and Remuneration Committee met four (4) times during FY 2025-26. The requisite quorum was present for all the meetings. Some of the important functions performed by the Nomination and Remuneration Committee include:

During FY 2025-26, the Composition of Nomination and Remuneration Committee was in line with Section 178(1) of the Companies Act, 2013, Regulation 19 of SEBI (LODR) Regulations, 2015 and DPE Guidelines. However, the Composition of Nomination and Remuneration Committee was not in line with Section 178(1) of the Companies Act, 2013, Regulation 19 of SEBI (LODR) Regulations, 2015 and DPE Guidelines w.e.f. 01 April 2025 to 20 May 2025 due to vacancies in the position of Independent Directors. As on 31 March 2026 the Company’s Nomination and Remuneration Committee consists of three (3) Independent Directors and Chairman & Managing Director. The Chairman of the Nomination and Remuneration Committee is an Independent Director. The Chairman of the Nomination and Remuneration Committee attended the 71st Annual General Meeting of the Company held on 28 August 2025. The terms of reference of
• Review management letters/letters of internal control weaknesses issued by the statutory auditors;
• Reviewing with the Management, the performance of statutory and internal auditors, the adequacy of internal control;
• Approval of appointment of a Chief Financial Officer after assessing the qualifications, experience and background, etc. of the candidate;

• Approval of appointment of a Chief Financial Officer after assessing the qualifications, experience and background, etc. of the candidate;
• Review the adequacy of the internal audit function, including the structure of the internal audit department, staffing and seniority of the official heading the department, reporting structure coverage and frequency of internal audit;
• Reviewing the utilisation of loans and/or advances from/ investment by the holding company in the subsidiary exceeding ` 100 Crore or 10% of the asset size of the subsidiary, whichever is lower, including existing loans/ advances/ investments;
• Recommending policy to the Board in line with the provisions of the Companies Act, 2013, DPE Guidelines and Presidential Directives/Guidelines issued by the Government of India from time to time;
• Discussion with internal auditors of any significant findings and follow-up thereon;
• Approval of Performance Related Pay to the employees of the Company;
• Appointment, removal and terms of remuneration of the chief internal auditor shall be subject to review by the audit committee;
• Review of the findings of any internal investigations by the internal auditors into matters where there is suspected fraud or irregularity or a failure of internal control systems of a material nature and reporting the matter to the Board;

Some of the important terms of reference of the Committee are as follows:
In pursuance to the provisions of Section 135 of the Companies Act, 2013, Rules made thereunder (as amended) and DPE Guidelines, Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) Committee has been constituted. However, the Composition of CSR Committee was not in terms of Section 135 of the Companies Act, 2013 w.e.f. 01 April 2025 to 20 May 2025 due to vacancies in position of Independent Directors. The salient terms of reference of the CSR Committee include reviewing the CSR Policy and making it more comprehensive to indicate the activities to be undertaken by the Company as specified under Schedule-VII of the Companies Act, 2013 and the DPE Guidelines as amended from time to time. The CSR Committee met four (4) times during FY 2025-26.
